  "description": "Winnovative HTML to PDF Library for .NET (Classic) can be used in .NET Framework, .NET Core and .NET Standard applications on Windows to convert HTML to PDF, images and SVG. The library can also create new PDF documents and edit, merge, split and fill existing PDF documents.\n\nFor Windows, Linux and macOS, on x64 and ARM64, Winnovative PDF Next offers a newer Chromium-based rendering engine for modern HTML, CSS and JavaScript in the multi-platform package Winnovative.Pdf.Next.HtmlToPdf and in the platform packages Winnovative.Pdf.Next.HtmlToPdf.Windows, Winnovative.Pdf.Next.HtmlToPdf.Windows.Arm64, Winnovative.Pdf.Next.HtmlToPdf.Linux, Winnovative.Pdf.Next.HtmlToPdf.Linux.Arm64 and Winnovative.Pdf.Next.HtmlToPdf.MacOS.\n\nThe full Winnovative PDF Next library, which also converts Word, Excel, RTF and Markdown to PDF, comes in the Winnovative.Pdf.Next, Winnovative.Pdf.Next.Windows, Winnovative.Pdf.Next.Windows.Arm64, Winnovative.Pdf.Next.Linux, Winnovative.Pdf.Next.Linux.Arm64 and Winnovative.Pdf.Next.MacOS packages.\n\nMigration guide from Classic to Next:\nhttps://www.winnovative-software.com/winnovative-classic-to-next-migration\n\nThe Winnovative.Pdf.Next.Compat.Classic package runs code written for the Classic library on the Next platform, with the same Winnovative namespace and classes.\n\nCompatibility:\n\n* .NET Framework 4.0 and above\n* .NET 10, 9, 8, 7, 6 and .NET Standard 2.0\n* Windows platforms\n* Azure Cloud Services and Azure Virtual Machines\n* Web, Console and Desktop applications\n\nMain Features:\n\n* Convert HTML with CSS3, SVG, web fonts and JavaScript to PDF\n* Create PDF links, forms, bookmarks and table of contents from HTML\n* Place HTML content in PDF pages, headers and footers\n* Convert HTML to JPEG, PNG and SVG images\n* Create PDF documents with text, graphics and images\n* Set PDF security and digital signatures\n* Edit, stamp, merge and split PDF documents",
  "iconFile": "images\\icon.png",
